New opt-in option `--modular-termination` (experimental): with it, `decreases {:global} E` declares a method's or function's global bound, and a call dispatched to a bodyless member of a trait whose implementations may lie in other modules must go to a smaller global bound, which rejects recursion through such traits that every module's call graph misses.  With `--show-hints` it reports every call that needs this rule.  Calls to known helpers and through function values are not yet checked.
